        text: 'A juice line is said to “lose capacity”. You start at the block flow diagram: tank farm, pasteuriser, buffer tank, filler. The PFD adds the detail: after the holding tube sits a divert valve that sends juice back to the balance tank (the small feed tank before the pasteuriser) whenever it is below its target temperature.\n\nThe stream table gives the design flow to the filler: 15,000 kg per hour. The trend shows the divert valve open for 5 minutes in every hour. Juice that is diverted goes round again instead of to the filler.\n\nSo the filler gets 15,000 × 55 / 60 = 13,750 kg per hour: 1,250 kg per hour less than design, without any machine being slow. The P&ID then gives you the tags of the divert valve and the temperature transmitter, so you can ask the right engineer why the temperature dips.',
