        ask: 'What syrup setpoint does the ratio station give now? And what would have happened to the mix if the syrup had stayed at a fixed 4 m³ per hour?',
        reveal: 'Ratio control: 19.8 / 5.5 = 3.6 m³ per hour, so the mix stays at 1 : 5.5.\n\nA fixed 4 m³ per hour would give 19.8 / 4 = 4.95 parts water per part syrup: a ratio of 1 : 4.95. That is about 11% more syrup per litre of water than the recipe, so the drink is too sweet, and costs more syrup, until someone notices.',
